comments.body:
Addressed the review feedback in `e55738af` and `84a05548`.

@hsliuustc0106:

1. Lifecycle: shutdown now closes the diffusion engine before waiting for dispatch tasks. Worker joins use one global 15-second deadline, followed by termination of all survivors and one global 5-second grace deadline. The previous code could spend the full timeout once per worker.
2. Multiprocess regression: `test_spawned_per_worker_queues_release_nested_numpy_shm` starts two real spawn children, creates one production queue and result pump per worker, transfers nested video/audio NumPy arrays through SHM, shuts down pumps, queues, and workers, then asserts every child exited and every SHM name is gone. The seven focused modules now report `145 passed` with no `resource_tracker` warning.
3. Reproduction: `examples/offline_inference/minimax_h3/dlo_dp2_lifecycle.py` now provides the exact two-GPU `dlo-dp2` and ordinary non-DLO TP2 `request` modes. The PR body contains the complete environment and commands, and explicitly states `enforce_eager=True`.
4. Baseline: the PR body now distinguishes literal parent `48298030`, which rejects the configuration, from archived head `64b19970`, which reproduces the greater-than-115-second hang.

@david6666666 request admission waiting is now configurable as requested. `request_batch_max_wait_ms=0` remains zero and disables waiting; a nonzero value such as the runner value of 500 ms explicitly enables coalescing.

@asukaqaq-s I agree that per-replica SP groups plus rank-local mmap sharing are the cleaner long-term topology. That redesign is intentionally out of this DP correctness PR. The current cross-DP AllGather path now accepts only requests with a complete matching scheduler compatibility key and fails closed on a partial-wave timeout, so an uncertain process group is never reused.
